# netsurf: table captions -- a table-wide block above or below the grid (roadmap WS-A Q3)
# Generated 2026-10-06
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser 59d7683099921fcc912d90e8cee1a139bae1ef3c (patch stack through 200)
#
# box_construct mapped display: table-caption to BOX_INLINE, so a
# <caption> reached box_normalise_table as an inline container among the
# table's children and was wrapped into an implied row group: its text
# became a cell in an extra first row, squeezed into column 1, with the
# table's border around it and caption-side ignored. Wikipedia's
# .wikitable captions, data tables on news and docs sites -- every
# captioned table rendered that way.
#
# Fix (the CSS table wrapper box, without a new box type):
#  - box_construct: table-caption maps to BOX_BLOCK. default.css gives
#    caption the UA's text-align: center.
#  - box_normalise_table: captions stay direct, unwrapped children of the
#    table, moved (in source order) ahead of the row groups and
#    normalised as blocks. box_inspect.h gains box_is_table_caption() and
#    box_table_row_groups() (the first child after the captions); every
#    walk over a table's row groups (normalise spans, column types,
#    min/max, layout_table's three passes) starts there, the implied row
#    for a caption-only table is appended after the captions, and
#    border-collapse's walk up the previous groups treats a caption like
#    the table's top edge.
#  - layout_minmax_table: each caption's minimum width bounds the
#    table's (CSS Tables 3 3.9.3, what every engine does), and
#    layout_table, once the column widths are picked, spreads any
#    shortfall between the grid and the widest caption minimum over the
#    columns -- the table itself grows, not just its min_width.
#  - layout_table: once the grid is laid out, layout_table_captions lays
#    each caption out as a block as wide as the table's border box and
#    stacks it above the border box (caption-side: top) or below it
#    (bottom). Captions stay children of the table, painted and hit-tested
#    like any child; layout_table_caption_extent gives the space they
#    take, and the callers make room: block flow moves the table down by
#    the top extent after its margin and clearance, and advances past the
#    bottom extent before the bottom margin collapses (so margins collapse
#    outside the captions, as with the wrapper box); a floated table adds
#    the extents to its margins, which float placement counts.
# Boundaries: absolutely positioned tables and tables laid out as flex or
# grid items reserve no caption space (the captions still lay out and
# paint, outside the table box); a caption's own width/height properties
# are ignored (it is always as wide as the table). The local relayout
# paths (163/165/198) decline any chain through a table (not a plain
# block), so content changes inside a caption take full layout.
#
# Test: testpages/pages/CSS-table-caption.html (CAPTION201, 8 checks,
# Chromium 8/8; measured spans are inline-blocks, since an inline
# element's rect here is still 0 wide -- a separate, older gap): top caption above the first row, as wide as the table,
# text centred, flow room above; caption-side: bottom below the grid with
# the next block after it; an unbreakable caption word widens the table;
# border-collapse table; caption-only table. Full gate: see
# docs/build-loop-state.md.
